## Assumptions and limitations
Primary comparator: Mpz, Mbp, Mag, Prx, Plp1, Cnp, Mal. Identity panel: Sox10, S100b, Erbb3, Dhh; proliferation: Mki67, Top2a, Pcna, Ccnb1, Cdk1, Mcm2; stress: Atf3, Jun, Ddit3, Hspa5, Hmox1, Nqo1 (individual genes always retained because heterogeneous pathways need not move together). Panels are analyst-prespecified biological controls, not direct TF activity assays. Gene symbol mappings require native source annotations; no orthology or assembly invented.

Within each eligible experiment compute Pmp22 change and change in its sample-level log-expression difference from mean myelin7. Biological-unit-based Welch or paired intervals only with verified replicate semantics; tiny/pool-limited designs get descriptive intervals or ranges, never cells-as-donors. Leave-one-marker and leave-one-unit checks assess stability, not replication. Expression baseline eligibility and normalization will be frozen before reading acquired target outcomes in panel-spec.json. Shared controls/source samples remain dependent across contrasts. Unknown or failed estimates stay missing/ineligible.

